   "label": "f01-two-schema-copies",
   "front": "npm run db:push runs a hand-written SQLite initializer instead of Prisma migrations. What are the consequences?",
   "back": "schema.prisma becomes a second copy kept in step by hand (the likeliest drift source); there are no migration files for the PostgreSQL move; and the initializer's PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON is per-connection, so it says nothing about the app's later connections.",
   "observation": "read-derived",
   "aiTag": false
  },
